-# Canonical Kronk wordmark for Rails-served pages.
-#
-# ONE source of truth for the 5-glyph sigil `ЖЯѺƝ₭`. Every surface
-# that renders the wordmark — SPA chrome, static-chrome top-band,
-# void masthead, landing hero, profile compose header — MUST render
-# through this partial (or its React sibling
-# `mastodon/features/ui/components/kronk_wordmark.tsx`). Drift in
-# glyph structure, font, colour, weight, or tracking = brand drift.
-#
-# Contract:
-#   - 5 individual `<span>` per glyph (per-character routing lives in
-#     the React sibling; static Rails renders a plain link).
-#   - `.kronk-wordmark` base class always present.
-#   - Optional `--<size>` modifier for size variants.
-#   - `aria-label="Kronk"`; glyphs `aria-hidden="true"`.
-#   - Wordmark string sourced from `t('kronk.signup.wordmark')` for
-#     consistency with the React component's `GLYPHS` array (both
-#     spell out ЖЯѺƝ₭).
-#
-# Locals:
-#   size: :chrome | :hero | :inline   (default :chrome)
-#     - :chrome — top-band identity; scales on hover (`transform:
-#       scale(1.03)`); hidden below 890px because the mobile chrome
-#       switches to a bottom tab-bar.
-#     - :hero — page focal element; large, centred; NO hover scale;
-#       visible on every viewport.
-#     - :inline — sits in a text run at 1em; no hover effect.
-#   href: URL (default '/kronk')
-#     - Anchor destination. `/kronk` is Rails-served — full-page nav.

- size = local_assigns.fetch(:size, :chrome)
- href = local_assigns.fetch(:href, '/kronk')

%a.kronk-wordmark{ class: "kronk-wordmark--#{size}", href: href, 'aria-label': 'Kronk' }
  - %w(Ж Я Ѻ Ɲ ₭).each do |glyph|
    %span.kronk-wordmark__char{ 'aria-hidden' => 'true' }= glyph
